<title>SOUTH AFRICA: S.Africa govt financing 456.1 mln rand in December.</title>
<headline>S.Africa govt financing 456.1 mln rand in December.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-01-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Government financing amounted to 456.1 million rand in December after it raised 1.63 billion rand in the bond markets while net short-term loans decreased by 1.18 billion rand, the Department of Finance said.</p>
<p>Government bonds and debentures totalling 15 billion rand and foreign loans of 748 million rand were redeemed during the financial year April to December 1996.</p>
<p>Total budgeted financing is 45.1 billion rand for the year (rand million)  -</p>
<p>				   Dec '96   Apl-Dec '96  Budgeted 96/97</p>
<p>Govt bonds and debentures  1,636.1   30,070.2	 39,604.7</p>
<p>Short-term (net):</p>
<p>  Bridging bonds		-696.0   -3,676.5	 -3,616.5</p>
<p>  Tender bills		   675.5    2,332.4	  3,616.5</p>
<p>  CPD			   -1,159.5    1,774.9	  3,000.0</p>
<p>Foreign loans		    ---	2,831.0	  2,500.0</p>
<p>Total financing		  456.1   33,332.0	 45,104.7</p>
<p>--Johannesburg newsroom, +27 11 482-1003</p>
